course: dictionary
lesson: 12182
title: Strong disapproval
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Condemnation is a noun. It comes from the verb condemn, which means to say that something is very wrong. When people or leaders say clearly that an action is bad, they make a condemnation. «The leaders made a strong condemnation of the attack on the school.» Strong condemnation means they spoke clearly and firmly against it.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. Words like attack, cruelty and war tell you the condemnation is about something terrible. Words like public, widespread and statement tell you that many people or countries are saying it openly.
explain: The word has two other meanings. In a court, a condemnation is the sentence a judge gives. «The judge's condemnation sent the thief to prison.» For a building, it is an official decision that the building is unsafe. «The council's condemnation of the old theatre meant nobody could go inside.»
fact: Condemnation means strong public disapproval: saying clearly that something is very wrong or bad.
fact: In law, a condemnation is the act of a court sentencing someone to a punishment.
fact: For a building, a condemnation is an official decision that it is unsafe and must not be used.
fact: «Widespread condemnation» means that many people or countries spoke out against something.
fact: Condemnation is mostly uncountable, so we usually say «strong condemnation», not «a strong condemnation» every time you use it in a list.
exercise: «Many countries made a widespread condemnation of the cruel attack.» What does condemnation mean here? | A gift for the injured | A new law about sport | *Strong public disapproval | A happy celebration of the attack
exercise: «The judge's condemnation sent the man to prison.» In this sentence, condemnation means: | A list of things to buy | A friendly greeting from the court | *A court sentencing someone to a punishment | Praise for good work
exercise: «The council's condemnation of the old school meant nobody could go inside.» What does this condemnation mean? | A plan to build a new park | A prize for the best school | *An official decision that the building is unsafe
test: Which word is closest in meaning to condemnation in «the strong condemnation of cruelty»? | Silence | Praise | *Disapproval | Joy
test: «The leaders issued a statement of condemnation after the war began.» What is a statement of condemnation? | A list of guests | A map of the battlefield | *A clear public statement saying something is very wrong | A song about the war
exam: Which sentence uses condemnation to mean an official decision that a building is unsafe? | «The judge's kind words made everyone smile.» | *«The council's condemnation closed the old theatre to the public.» | «The crowd gave a loud cheer for the team.» | «The leaders made a strong condemnation of the war.»
